      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Error bars are graphical elements placed on bar charts (and other types of plots) to visually represent the variability or uncertainty in data. They help visualize how much the individual data points typically deviate from the central tendency (e.g., mean) represented by the bar."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Types of error bars"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The two most common ways to sketch errors bars for a bar chart are:"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Range error bars"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Range error bars use the smallest (minimum) and greatest (maximum) data points in a set for each bar. The bar extends from the minimum to the maximum value, illustrating the full spread of the data."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Standard deviation (SD) error bars"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Standard deviation error bars show the average distance of each data point from the mean. On a bar chart, each bar represents a group mean. Standard deviation error bars extend above and below the mean value of a dataset by one or more standard deviations (±SD).",
            "bold": [
              "Standard deviation error bars",
              "above and below the mean"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Steps to sketch error bars on a bar chart"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The researchers are measuring the average plant height (cm) in three different light conditions. They grow bean plants in three groups:"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group A: Low light",
            "bold": [
              "Group A"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group B: Medium light",
            "bold": [
              "Group B"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group C: High light",
            "bold": [
              "Group C"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "After four weeks they measure the heights of the plants."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Heights (cm) of the bean plants after four weeks",
            "header": [
              "",
              "Group A",
              "Group B",
              "Group C"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Plant 1",
                "10",
                "14",
                "18"
              ],
              [
                "Plant 2",
                "11",
                "16",
                "20"
              ],
              [
                "Plant 3",
                "9",
                "15",
                "19"
              ]
            ],
            "bold": [
              "Plant 1",
              "Plant 2",
              "Plant 3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 1: Calculate the mean of each group",
            "bold": [
              "Step 1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group A Mean of = (10 + 11 + 9)/3 = 10 cm"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group B Mean of= (14 + 16 + 15)/3 = 15 cm"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group C Mean of= (18 + 20 + 19)/3 = 19 cm"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The bars on the bar chart are drawn at heights 10, 15, and 19 for Groups A, B, and C, respectively."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 2: Calculate the spread",
            "bold": [
              "Step 2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A) For SD error bars:",
            "bold": [
              "A) For SD error bars"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group A: SD ≈ 1 (Data: 10, 11, 9)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group B: SD ≈ 1 (Data: 14, 16, 15)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group C: SD ≈ 1 (Data: 18, 20, 19)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "B) For range error bars:",
            "bold": [
              "B) For range error bars"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group A: min = 9, max = 11"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group B: min = 14, max = 16"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group C: min = 18, max = 20"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 3: Draw the error bars",
            "bold": [
              "Step 3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "SD error bars: Start at the mean (top of each bar), extend up and down by 1 cm (Mean ±1 SD).",
            "bold": [
              "SD error bars"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group A: from 9 (10-1) to 11 (10+1)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group B: from 14 (15-1) to 16 (15+1)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Group C: from 18 (19-1) to 20 (19+1)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Range error bars: Extend from the minimum to maximum value for each group.",
            "bold": [
              "Range error bars"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Add a horizontal cap at each end of the vertical error bar for clarity."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table: Statistical summary of plant measurements",
            "header": [
